\subsection{\label{hspice using verilogA}HSPICE using Verilog A}
\vspace{-4mm}
The obtained resistance values from the electrical readout as described in \ref{electrical readout} are utilized in the circuit-level simulation of the ReLU max-pooling circuit using Verilog A. In the HSPICE simulation of a single ReLU, the obtained resistance values act as a variable resistor connected to a constant resistor~(R\textsubscript{1}) of value 58.954~K$\Omega$, creating a voltage divider. The output from the divider is fed as an input to the CMOS inverter pair based on the 16nm node of the predictive technology model~(PTM).
A 9-input interconnection of such ReLU circuits with an interconnect network consisting of resistors and NMOS transistors is implemented in HSPICE to obtain the combined result of the ReLU-max pooling function.
